flowchart TB
    accTitle: Reasoning and retrieval flexibly support planning
    accDescr: Reasoning and retrieval are internal actions that can support proposal, evaluation, and selection. The figure shows multiple possible relationships and deliberately does not prescribe a single order among the planning sub-stages.

    REASON[Reasoning<br/>process working information]
    RETRIEVE[Retrieval<br/>read from long-term memory]
    subgraph PLANNING[Planning responsibilities]
      direction LR
      PROP[Proposal]
      EVAL[Evaluation]
      SELECT[Selection]
    end
    FLEX[Flexible support<br/>not a fixed schedule]
    REASON --> PROP
    REASON --> EVAL
    REASON --> SELECT
    RETRIEVE --> PROP
    RETRIEVE --> EVAL
    RETRIEVE --> SELECT
    PLANNING -.-> FLEX

    classDef process fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef action fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    classDef note fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.3px;
    class REASON,RETRIEVE,PROP,EVAL,SELECT process;
    class FLEX note;
